d Safra","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.737938,"lo":7.423419,"d":220,"ds":"The Synagogue Edmond Safra is an Orthodox Jewish congregation and synagogue, located at 15 avenue de la Costa, in Monte Carlo, in Monaco. The synagogue is run by the Association Cultuelle Israelite de Monaco (ACIM). The synagogue is one of several that are eponymous with Edmond J. Safra (1932-1999), a banker and philanthropist, partially or fully funded by the Edmond J. Safra Foundation.","wpu":"Synagogue Edmond Safra","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Monaco_Synagogue_4.jpg/960px-Monaco_Synagogue_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Théâtre Princesse Grace","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.7377,"lo":7.426,"d":248,"ds":"The Théâtre Princesse Grace is a theatre in Monaco.","wpu":"Théâtre Princesse Grace","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Entr%C3%A9e_du_th%C3%A9%C3%A2tre_Princesse_Grace_et_du_cin%C3%A9ma_des_Beaux-Arts_%28Monaco%29.jpg/960px-Entr%C3%A9e_du_th%C3%A9%C3%A2tre_Princesse_Grace_et_du_cin%C3%A9ma_des_Beaux-Arts_%28Monaco%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sainte-Dévote Chapel","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":43.737506,"lo":7.420976,"d":295,"ds":"The Chapel of Sainte—Dévote (French: Chapelle Sainte Dévote; Ligurian: Geija de Santa Devotâ) is a Roman Catholic chapel dedicated to Saint Devota, the patron saint of Monaco, which lies in the Monégasque ward of Ravin de Sainte-Dévote. The chapel was first mentioned in archived documents dated 1070, built against the wall of Vallon des Gaumates, on the space now occupied by the Chapel of Relics.","wpu":"Sainte-Dévote Chapel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/%C3%89glise_de_Saint-D%C3%A9vote_Monaco_IMG_1202.jpg/960px-%C3%89glise_de_Saint-D%C3%A9vote_Monaco_IMG_1202.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Monaco-Monte-Carlo station (French: Gare de Monaco-Monte-Carlo; Monégasque: Staçiun de Munegu-Munte-Carlu) is the sole railway station in the Principality of Monaco, though part of it is located in Beausoleil, France. It is served by trains of the French state-owned operator SNCF, on the Marseille–Ventimiglia railway line. The station, along with the entire railway line in the principality, is located underground.","wpu":"Monaco–Monte-Carlo station","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Monaco_Monte-Carlo_Train_Station_%2849800541117%29.jpg/960px-Monaco_Monte-Carlo_Train_Station_%2849800541117%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}